## Cleaning `gene_symbol`

This section removes the specified symbols `(`, `)`, `%`, `*`, `$`, `|`, `｜`, `&`, `#`, and `.` from `gene_symbol`. The original letter case is preserved, and changed values are recorded for review.
```{r}

##gene_symbol
# Restore the original gene symbols from wide_data
i <- match(clean_wide_data$source_file, wide_data$source_file)
clean_wide_data$gene_symbol <- wide_data$gene_symbol[i]

# Save the original values for comparison
gene_symbol_before <- clean_wide_data$gene_symbol

# Remove only the specified symbols; keep letter case unchanged
clean_wide_data$gene_symbol <- gsub(
  "[()%*\\$|｜&#.]",
  "",
  trimws(clean_wide_data$gene_symbol)
)

# Show the values that changed
symbol_changes <- data.frame(
  source_file = clean_wide_data$source_file,
  gene_accession_id = clean_wide_data$gene_accession_id,
  before = gene_symbol_before,
  after = clean_wide_data$gene_symbol
)

symbol_changes <- symbol_changes[
  !is.na(symbol_changes$before) &
    symbol_changes$before != symbol_changes$after,
]

View(symbol_changes)

```


